preConditionHook:
// Entry & Exit Confessions bonus #2 (Day Of Week, With A Twist), verbatim:
// long on Thursday's bar (fills Friday's open), short on Friday's bar (fills
// Monday's open), gated on the strategy's own equity not having lost more
// than lossAmt over the last lookback bars. 'next bar at open' and 'next bar
// at market' are the same fill here.
// The book: TotEquity = NetProfit + OpenPositionProfit, an EL VARIABLE, and
// TotEquity[lookback] reads that variable's own history -- which holds its
// initial 0 for every bar before the strategy's first evaluated one (the EL
// warm-up convention; BarRangeAboveStd is the reference). So for the first
// lookback evaluated bars the test is against 0 equity, not against a value
// recomputed from bars EL never saw. Mirrored with a zero-initialised ring
// buffer whose slot at the cursor was written exactly lookback bars ago;
// re-seeded if the length ever changes.
totEquity = ctx.NetProfit() + ctx.OpenPositionProfit();
if ((int)lookback < 1) {
    pastEquity = totEquity;
} else {
    if (equityHistory.size() != (std::size_t)(int)lookback) {
        equityHistory.assign((std::size_t)(int)lookback, 0.0);
        equityCursor = 0;
    }
    pastEquity = equityHistory[equityCursor];
    equityHistory[equityCursor] = totEquity;
    equityCursor = (equityCursor + 1) % equityHistory.size();
}
// EL DayOfWeek(Date): 0 = Sunday .. 6 = Saturday, of the bar's wall-clock
// close date (EL_Date_Probe.txt, 169/169 incl. evening bars). day_of_week()
// in time.h uses the same numbering.
dow = day_of_week(day_of(ctx.Time(0)));
